Main ingredients: 500g pork belly, 50g water chestnuts, 300g Cantonese bok choy

Additional ingredients: 50g cornflour, 20g white pepper powder, 20g Hua Diao wine/yellow rice wine, salt, spring onions, spring onions, ginger to taste

1. Slice the pork belly thinly, then mince finely into a bowl. Dice the water chestnuts and set aside.

2. Vigorously knead the pork in the bowl, gradually adding scallion and ginger water in small amounts—avoid over-moistening. Continue kneading until the mixture becomes slightly sticky and forms cohesive balls without collapsing.

3. Incorporate the cornflour, diced water chestnuts, half the white pepper powder, and salt. Mix thoroughly.

4. Fill a pot with a generous amount of water and bring to a vigorous boil. Shape the prepared mixture into balls slightly larger than the palm of your hand and add to the pot. Take care not to stir or disturb the meatballs, as this may cause them to disintegrate before setting.

5. Add the remaining white pepper, spring onions, spring onions, and cooking wine. Bring to a rolling boil over high heat for 1 minute, skimming off any foam that rises to the surface.

6. Reduce heat to low and simmer for 10 minutes. Add the washed Cantonese bok choy.

7. Continue simmering over low heat for a further 10 minutes before serving.
